{"datasource.applyTemplateVariables may mutate the passed query object, which can unintentionally mutate request.targets for the remainder of the request lifecycle. Consider ensuring applyTemplateVariables operates on a clone, or clone the query before passing it in.": 0.3122614622116089, "The filter order differs between split paths: one path filters by expr before filtering out hidden queries. It's safer/clearer to consistently drop hidden queries first to avoid running templating/interpolation work on hidden queries.": 0.17784404754638672, "The new applyTemplateVariables mocks mutate and return the same LokiQuery object instead of returning a new object. This can hide real-world issues around immutability and make call-count expectations brittle. Prefer returning a new object (e.g., { ...query, expr: ... }).": 0.24356406927108765}